        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "rac-3-Aminopropane-1,2-diol (23 mg, 0.25 mmol) and 2-hydroxybenzaldehyde (26 μL, 0.25 mmol) were refluxed in methanol (18 mL) for 2 h to form rac-H3L in situ. Dy(CH3COO)3·3H2O (157 mg, 0.40 mmol), (nBu4N)4Mo8O26 (50 mg, 0.023 mmol), NH3·H2O (34 μL, 0.60 mmol), and CH3COONH4 (123 mg, 1.6 mmol) were added with stirring at room temperature. After 30 min the mixture was sealed in a 23 mL Teflon-lined Parr bomb, heated at 70 °C for 12 h, and cooled to 30 °C at 4 °C h−1. The filtrate was layered with n-hexane to give pale-yellow block crystals.",
